# A desktop kernel: no server, datacenter or broadcast-TV hardware (docs/STACK.md S13 and 2.11, change 10). Each line
# turns off a menu or a driver, and the subtree under it goes with it (kconfig.sh check refuses the build if
# something still selects one of them). Kept on purpose: SCSI for virtual machines (virtio, VMware PVSCSI and LSI
# Logic, Hyper-V, Xen, QEMU's LSI 53c895a), the iSCSI initiator, 10 GbE NICs found in desktops (Intel ixgbe, i40e;
# Broadcom tg3; Marvell), and the Wi-Fi and camera drivers from staging that laptops use (rtl8723bs, atomisp, ipu3).

# InfiniBand and RDMA (and NVMe and iSCSI over RDMA)
# CONFIG_INFINIBAND is not set
# SCSI and NVMe target (storage servers)
# CONFIG_TARGET_CORE is not set
# CONFIG_NVME_TARGET is not set
# Fibre Channel
# CONFIG_NVME_FC is not set
# CONFIG_LIBFC is not set
# CONFIG_FCOE is not set
# CONFIG_FCOE_FNIC is not set
# SCSI host bus adapters (RAID and SAS controllers)
# CONFIG_SCSI_CXGB3_ISCSI is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_CXGB4_ISCSI is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_BNX2_ISCSI is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_BNX2X_FCOE is not set
# CONFIG_BE2ISCSI is not set
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_3W_XXXX_RAID is not set
